.TH SPINDLE-CONFIG-HELPER 1 "October 2026" "Spindle 0.13" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spindle-config-helper \- generate and validate Spindle configuration files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spindle-config-helper
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fISPINDLE_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spindle-config-helper
is a utility for generating and validating Spindle configuration files in HPC
environments. It analyzes the local system to automatically detect optimal
configuration settings and outputs a
.I spindle.conf
file suitable for the environment.
.PP
The tool performs the following analysis:
.IP \(bu 2
Detects local vs. remote filesystem mounts (NFS, Lustre, GPFS, tmpfs)
.IP \(bu 2
Validates
.B $TMPDIR
availability and recommends appropriate paths
.IP \(bu 2
Tests SSH connectivity to verify compute node access
.IP \(bu 2
Discovers Python installations via system PATH
.IP \(bu 2
Generates
.I localprefix
from top-level directories without remote mounts
.IP \(bu 2
Validates path writability and accessibility
.PP
The tool should be run on compute nodes in the same environment where
Spindle will execute, as login/front-end nodes may have different characteristics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display detailed usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIFILE\fR
Write output to
.I FILE
instead of stdout. By default, fails if
.I FILE
already exists.
.TP
.BR \-\-overwrite
Allow overwriting an existing output file when used with
.BR \-o .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check [=\fIFILE\fR]
Validate an existing
.I spindle.conf
file. Checks option names against the current Spindle version, validates
enum values, and reports unknown or deprecated options. If
.I FILE
is not specified, only validates options passed after
.BR \-\- .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Generate a complete configuration file including all Spindle options.
Options with default values are commented out (prefixed with '#').
Options specified after
.B \-\-
are uncommented. Useful for discovering available options.
.TP
.BR \-\-usage
Display Spindle's usage summary with all available configuration options.
.SH MODES
.SS Default Mode
Without any mode flags,
.B spindle-config-helper
generates a minimal configuration with four essential path variables:
.TP
.B commpaths
Local directories for inter-process communication. Prefers
.B $TMPDIR
if set, otherwise recommends a suitable local filesystem like
.I /tmp
or
.IR /dev/shm .
.TP
.B cachepaths
Local directories for file caching. Uses similar logic to
.BR commpaths .
.TP
.B pythonprefix
Python installation directories discovered via
.B which python
and
.BR "which python3" .
Validates that
.I bin/python
or
.I bin/python3
exists under each directory.
.TP
.B localprefix
Colon-separated list of top-level directories that should be excluded from
caching. Generated from
.I /proc
.I /sys
.I /dev
and other top-level directories without remote mounts underneath.
.PP
The output includes warnings and recommendations as comments.
.SS Check Mode
When invoked with
.BR \-c ,
the tool validates an existing configuration file:
.IP \(bu 2
Parses
.I key = value
pairs from the file
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies option names are valid in the current Spindle version
.IP \(bu 2
Validates enum values (e.g., level must be high/medium/low/off)
.IP \(bu 2
Reports malformed lines, unknown options, and invalid values
.IP \(bu 2
Command-line options passed after
.B \-\-
take precedence over config file values
.SS All Mode
When invoked with
.BR \-a ,
the tool enumerates all Spindle configuration options (~49 options).
Options with default values are commented out, while options specified
on the command line after
.B \-\-
are uncommented with their specified values.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Preferred directory for
.B commpaths
and
.BR cachepaths .
If not set, the tool recommends
.I /tmp
or another suitable local filesystem.
.TP
.B SANDBOX_ENGINE
If set, indicates the tool is running in a sandbox environment.
Affects capability testing (e.g., Munge daemon connectivity cannot be
verified in a sandbox).
.SH SPINDLE OPTIONS
Any valid Spindle configuration option can be passed after
.BR \-\- .
Use
.B spindle-config-helper \-\- \-\-usage
to see all available options. Common options include:
.TP
.BI \-\-commpaths= PATHS
Colon-separated list of directories for inter-process communication.
Should be on local (not remote) filesystems.
.TP
.BI \-\-cachepaths= PATHS
Colon-separated list of directories for file caching.
Should be on local filesystems with sufficient space.
.TP
.BI \-\-level= LEVEL
Aggressiveness of library redistribution:
.BR high ", " medium ", " low ", " off ", or " default .
.TP
.BI \-\-security= MODE
Security mode:
.BR none ", " munge ", " keyfile ", or " launchmon .
.TP
.BI \-\-launcher= TYPE
Resource manager:
.BR serial ", " slurm ", " flux ", " lsf ", " alps ", " openmpi ", " wreckrun ", " jsrun ", " hostbin ", or " srun .
.TP
.BI \-\-python\-prefix= PATHS
Colon-separated list of Python installation prefixes.
.TP
.BI \-\-local\-prefix= PATHS
Colon-separated list of directory prefixes to exclude from caching.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate a new configuration to stdout:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper
.RE
.fi
.TP
Generate and save to file:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper -o ~/.spindle/spindle.conf
.RE
.fi
.TP
Generate with custom paths:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper -- --commpaths=/dev/shm --cachepaths=/tmp
.RE
.fi
.TP
Check existing config for warnings:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper -c ~/.spindle/spindle.conf | grep WARNING
.RE
.fi
.TP
Update existing config with new security setting:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper -c ~/.spindle/spindle.conf \\
  -o ~/.spindle/spindle.conf --overwrite \\
  -- --security=munge
.RE
.fi
.TP
Generate complete config with all options:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper -a -o spindle.conf.full
.RE
.fi
.TP
Generate config with high aggressiveness:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper -a -- --level=high --launcher=slurm
.RE
.fi
.TP
View all available Spindle options:
.nf
.RS
spindle-config-helper -- --usage
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/spindle.conf
System-wide Spindle configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.spindle/spindle.conf
Per-user Spindle configuration file (common location).
.TP
.I /proc/mounts
Used to detect filesystem mount points and types.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Valid configuration was generated or validated.
.TP
.B 1
Error. Invalid arguments, file I/O error, or configuration parse error occurred.
.SH NOTES
.SS Path Validation
The tool validates paths by checking:
.IP \(bu 2
Parent directory is writable
.IP \(bu 2
Path is on a local (not remote) filesystem
.IP \(bu 2
Path can be created and deleted (test file creation)
.PP
Paths that fail validation are filtered out and reported in warnings.
.SS SSH Testing
The tool tests SSH connectivity to the local hostname to verify that
compute node access is properly configured. This test uses
.BR "ssh -o BatchMode=yes"
to check for key-based authentication without password prompts.
.SS Python Discovery
Python installations are discovered by running
.B which python
and
.BR "which python3" ,
following symlinks to find the actual installation directories.
The tool validates that
.I bin/python
or
.I bin/python3
exists under each discovered prefix.
.SS Sandbox Environments
When running in a sandbox environment (detected via
.BR SANDBOX_ENGINE ),
some tests are limited. For example, Munge daemon connectivity cannot
be verified, though Munge binary availability is still checked.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spindle (1)
.PP
Spindle documentation: https://github.com/hpc/Spindle
